# Borderless design

The user prefers **borderless** layouts for TraderMemos.

## Do

- Unify page chrome on `bg-bg` (sidebar, header, main content)
- Separate sections with spacing, type hierarchy, and subtle hover (`bg-bg-hover`)
- Use elevation only for true overlays (modals, popovers, dropdowns)
- Keep borders on inputs, buttons, and chips where interaction affordance needs them

## Avoid

- `border-b` / `border-t` on shell header, nav bands, full-bleed panels, settings rows
- Box borders around every list item or section card
- Inset divider shadows between nav and main (`shadow-[inset_1px_0_0_…]`) unless explicitly requested
- Hairline grids on data tables when hover + density is enough

## Card blocks (page layout)

- Wrap route content in `<Page>` — void background, `gap-4`, padding
- Each logical section gets a `<Card>` — borderless `bg-bg-panel`, optional title/action
- Use `flush` on cards that contain tables or full-bleed lists
- Use `fill` when a card should grow in a column layout

## When DESIGN.md conflicts

`DESIGN.md` mentions hairline bento gaps and panel borders — treat those as optional structure, not mandatory boxes. Prefer the user's borderless direction unless they ask for explicit dividers.
